SM(446,{"n":"Acts 1","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Acts 1.mp3","d":2656.0,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest, serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.64,"So we'll go ahead and get started here in the Book of Acts, chapter 1, verse 1."],[28.48,"And here we have the dedication I mentioned."],[31.6,"The former account I made, O Theophilus, of all that Jesus began both to do and teach until the day in which he was taken up after he through the Holy Spirit had given commandments to the apostles whom he had chosen."],[48.48,"So we hear about the former account that's referring to the gospel according to St."],[53.04,"Luke. The first volume."],[55.22,"And he sort of summarizes it."],[57.46,"Notice he summarizes it as. all that Jesus began both to do and to teach"],[66.14,"Well, Jesus has ascended into heaven."],[69.15,"So the book of Acts is not going to be more of Jesus doing and teaching things directly."],[76.03,"But this is part of that right from the get-go, where Saint Luke is setting up, what the apostles are now going to do and to teach are really the Acts and the Deeds of the teachings of Christ."],[89.15,"Because again, they're his representatives."],[92.11,"And so the work that Christ is doing in the world, the work of salvation continues through the apostles."],[98.53,"Whom he chose, I remember what apostle means. whom he chose and who he sent out to do this"],[108.77,"So uh the the church, the life of the church going forward, from St."],[114.05,"Luke's perspective, is a continuation of Christ's mission and and teaching and work."],[120.45,"It's not sort of a separate thing."],[122.39,"Where we have Israel and then we have Jesus and then we have church right here afterwards, but this is a continuation."],[132.39,"This is a continuation."],[135.59,"This also argues against the uh the whole red letter idea."],[140.77,"Because according to this here in St."],[142.45,"Luke, what St."],[143.33,"Paul is going to preach, what St."],[144.93,"Peter is going to teach, what St."],[146.05,"James is. going to teach here and Acts the Apostles, are the teachings of Christ"],[150.89,"They're not something new or added to or different."],[159.29,"To whom he also presented himself alive after his suffering by many infallible proofs, being seen by them during 40 days and speaking of the things pertaining to the kingdom of God."],[171.69,"So here we once again have Saint Luke's appeal again to evidence."],[181.1,"The evidence that Jesus was raised from the dead is what?"],[185.42,"That for 40 days, the apostles saw him afterwards."],[188.95,"s. And he presented to them many infallible proof"],[195.28,"It wasn't just, oh, they had some visions."],[198.64,"I mean, this is something that was common in the ancient world."],[201.44,"People do about this."],[202.4,"It happens today."],[204.08,"Where people will say they have seen some loved one who has passed away."],[208.56,"They'll say, I swear I saw him."],[211.12,"You know, I saw him in my bedroom, or I saw him, you know, somewhere where we used to go."],[216.85,"That happened in the ancient world too."],[218.85,"And what St."],[219.49,"Luke is trying to tell us is that's not what I'm talking about."],[222.95,"He he showed them infallible proofs that it was really him and he was really alive."],[226.87,"At the end of St."],[227.75,"Luke's gospel, this is one of the things that he really hammers home."],[232.07,"Because it's in St."],[232.87,"Luke's gospel, Jesus appears and he says, Look."],[236.93,"See my hands and my feet."],[239.25,"He shows them the wounds."],[240.94,"He says, Look."],[242.06,"He says, handle me and see."],[244.08,"Because a spirit does not have flesh and blood, as you can see that I have."],[247.76,"So St. Luke is really hammering on this."],[249.76,"This isn't a ghost."],[251.38,"This isn't a hallucination because they're all sad."],[254.18,"You know that Jesus died."],[255.86,"He was there."],[256.82,"They touched him."],[258.12,"They handle he had flesh and bones."],[260.12,"Jesus then goes on to eat with them."],[262.9,"He eats food in front of them."],[264.5,"So St. Luke is really making this point."],[266.42,"He's going to refer back to it later in Acts too."],[268.98,"But that's what he's referring to when he says, by many infallible proofs."],[272.31,"Jesus died and then he was alive again."],[275.35,"They all did"],[283.07,"They all saw."],[283.95,"They all did."],[284.91,"And uh St."],[285.87,"Paul is gonna hammer that home even more because he's gonna give this huge list of people who saw Jesus."],[290.91,"And then he's gonna say, at one point he appeared to 500 people at once."],[295.33,"And he said, St."],[296.21,"Paul's gonna say, Many of them are still alive, you can go ask them."],[300.61,"If you don't, if you don't take my word for it."],[303.25,"But so St."],[303.89,"Luke is very much here in that same spirit of saying, you know, that's I'm talking about history, I'm talking about reality, not visions and stuff."],[313.49,"Jesus was dead, buried in a tomb, and then he was alive again."],[318.13,"His body was standing up, and he was. alive, eating, talking, walking for 40 days"],[330.33,"Being assembled together with them, he commanded them not to depart from Jerusalem, but to wait for the promise of the Father, which he said, You have heard from me, for John truly baptized with water, but you shall be baptized with the Holy Spirit not many days from now."],[347.69,"So St. Lucas said that during that resurrection period, when he appeared to them, he was teaching them about the kingdom."],[356.41,"And we've seen we saw some of that at the end of the Gospel of Luke"],[360.49,"Remember, as he was walking on the road to Emmaus at the end of Luke's gospel, Jesus explained from all the law and the prophets."],[366.95,"All of the things concerning himself."],[369.59,"So he's, you know, during his life, we saw Jesus use parables a lot, you know, and people didn't understand."],[376.63,"Uh, we saw in when we just finished St."],[379.35,"John's Gospel, we saw there, even the disciples who were there with him."],[382.63,"And in St."],[383.27,"John's Gospel, he speaks relatively plainly."],[386.71,"They all were clueless."],[389.24,"But we what we see after the resurrection, and we see that throughout the gospels, is that we didn't understand until the resurrection."],[397.32,"So during this 40 days, it's not just that Jesus is appearing and saying, Look, I'm really alive, but that he's then sort of now they're sort of getting it."],[406.76,"You know, and he's finishing the teaching."],[408.44,"And the final part of that is Jesus' directive to them."],[412.96,"You know, he's sending them out, but don't go yet."],[416.7,"But wait, because the Holy Spirit is coming."],[421.86,"And he refers them all the way back to the very beginning of his ministry with St."],[425.94,"John the foreigner, St."],[427.54,"John the Baptist."],[429.0,"Remember when St."],[429.8,"John said, I baptize with water, but one is coming who will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire."],[435.82,"He's referring back to that promise."],[438.88,"Is now going to be fulfilled."],[440.88,"And so wait here, wait here until that happens."],[445.76,"Now, in terms of how they would have understood that, this is something that was promised in the prophets."],[454.44,"In Joel chapter 2, which we're going to see, St."],[457.16,"Peter is going to preach a sermon about."],[459.88,"That's on the day of Pentecost when it happens."],[463.06,"God says that in those last days I'll pour out my spirit on all flesh."],[468.82,"And in the book of Ezekiel, when God is talking about the new covenant he's going to issue, he says, I'm going to place my spirit in you."],[479.22,"So this is a promise for the last days, for the new covenant, for what's to come once the Messiah has come."],[486.42,"And so that's how they would have."],[489.7,"Jesus has we know, according to St."],[491.62,"Luke, but going through the Old Testament scriptures with them and explaining them."],[495.46,"And so he's saying, This promise, not just that you heard from St."],[499.82,"John, not just that you received from me, but this promise from you know centuries past is now going to come to fruition."],[512.14,"Therefore, when they had come together, they asked him, saying, Lord, will you at this time restore the kingdom to Israel?"],[520.7,"Now you may think this is a sign that they don't get it."],[524.47,"Oh, they're still on with this."],[526.15,"Oh, we need a kingdom here in Israel."],[529.59,"But, but um this question makes sense based on those prophecies I just mentioned."],[538.55,"Those prophecies I just mentioned about the new covenant in Jeremiah and Ezekiel and in Joel all also talk about the kingdom of God being established."],[550.19,"So the fact that Christ has told them this prophecy concerning the Spirit of God, this prophecy concerning the Holy Spirit is about to come true."],[558.51,"It's a logical question for them to ask."],[560.75,"Oh, is this other part right going to come true?"],[567.31,"And notice Jesus' answer here."],[568.99,"And he said to them, It is not for you to know times or seasons which the Father has put in his own authority, but you shall receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you, and you shall be witnesses to me in Jerusalem and in all Judea and Samaria and to the ends of the earth."],[585.07,"So Jesus doesn't say you still don't get it"],[590.93,"Jesus doesn't say, My kingdom is not of this world, there is no kingdom."],[595.07,"He says, It's not for you to know when."],[598.59,"It's not for you to know when."],[600.75,"So what Jesus is talking about here, what the disciples are asking about now that they understand, is not about, okay, so now you're going to overthrow the Romans."],[611.09,"That's not what they're asking."],[613.89,"But the kingdom of God, which already exists."],[619.12,"Which is the kingdom that Christ rules over."],[621.46,"He's about to be enthroned after his ascension as a king over the kingdom of God."],[631.23,"And is real and is manifest in the church."],[634.19,"It's manifest wherever Christ is."],[636.75,"But the kingdoms of this world still exist too."],[639.79,"At that time, Rome still existed."],[642.83,"To this day, the kingdoms of this world and the kingdoms of this world, by and large, are opposed to the kingdom of God and to Christ."],[650.99,"And so what they're talking about when they say restore the kingdom of Israel is they're talking about the end."],[658.83,"They're talking about that time when the kingdom of God is going to become the whole world, when heaven and earth are going to come together."],[666.75,"The kingdom of heaven and earth are going to come together and become one, the day of Christ's return."],[673.83,"And so there is a certain misunderstanding from them in that they don't understand that there's going to be the separation in time and how long it's going to be between Christ's resurrection and the end."],[688.95,"So ultimately what they're asking here is now the time, then."],[693.13,"Because as I just quoted the book of Joel, in those last days, then that's what I will pour out by spirit."],[699.42,"So they're okay."],[700.22,"Well, these are the last days."],[701.26,"Well, how many last days are there before?"],[704.98,"And we'll see later on, uh, St."],[707.94,"Paul and other New Testament writers will refer to the present time as the last days."],[713.62,"So whenever you see one of those folks saying, Are we living in the end times?"],[717.26,"The answer is yes."],[718.94,"But we've been living in the end times for 1980 years."],[726.06,"So this is the last, this is the last age of the earth before the age to come."],[736.14,"So that's the question."],[738.78,"Jesus tells them you don't get to know how long this is going to be."],[745.1,"He says, but this is what you need to know."],[748.36,"When the Spirit comes, you will receive power, and you will go out and be my be my witnesses."],[756.52,"And then he lays out the plan for what. we're gonna see in the rest of the book of the Acts of the Apostles"],[763.68,"You're gonna be my witnesses in Jerusalem."],[766.77,"Starting right here, in the city of Jerusalem, and then all Judea, the Roman province, and then Samaria, the neighboring Roman province, and then to the ends of the earth."],[781.76,"And then to the whole world."],[784.96,"So this is in a way setting out the plan."],[788.26,"And Jesus is saying, This is what you don't need to know when I'm gonna judge the living of the dead."],[792.9,"What you need to know is, this is your mission."],[796.28,"This is what you're to do, this is what's set before you."],[799.8,"And this could be an important message for us"],[803.76,"Because we a lot of times, not just with all the end time speculation you get of people saying, oh, Jesus is going to return on this date."],[812.58,"I know it."],[813.14,"You know, back in 2012, the mind calendar is ending so clearly."],[816.74,"And in the year 2000, oh, it's the year 2000, you know, and then you know, over and over again through human history, people have picked these dates and they've come and gone."],[825.54,"And I've lived through 10 or 12 ends of the world."],[829.3,"So but not just that, not just that we shouldn't engage in that idol speculation."],[835.3,"But you know, we have we have a tendency, especially as very sort of cerebral westerners, and as people who live in the modern world where we have a lot of technology, so we all have a lot of free time on our hands to sit around and do oh compared to the ancient world?"],[850.06,"You want to do farm work from sunup till sundown, and then uh Pierre may do that, but if you're doing farm work from sunup till sundown and taking care of five or six kids and you know, the the whole shebang your whole life until you're doing the farmers and making all the meals and churning the butter and from sunup till sundown every day until you drop dead."],[873.82,"And when that's your life, you don't have a lot of time to sit around and speculate about when the end of the world is going to come."],[879.58,"No, or much of anything else."],[882.78,"Nowadays we can go and argue about things on Facebook and you know, all kinds of do all kinds of silly things with all our free time."],[891.66,"But we have this temptation then to sit and want to speculate, come up with theories, you know, pry into things, you know, have these huge debates where you know churches divide over whether it was six literal 24-hour days in the book of Genesis or whether it was periods of time or whether it was this or that."],[915.86,"You know, we get all involved in these things."],[918.66,"You know, we get involved in these things, and they're a distraction."],[923.14,"They're a distraction."],[924.98,"What does the Lord really require of us?"],[928.23,"What does God put us here to do?"],[930.07,"We know what those things are, they're pretty straightforward."],[934.31,"And these other things are a distraction from that."],[936.55,"This is why St"],[939.39,"Paul later is going to say, you know, don't get involved in genealogies and all myths and all these, you know, philosophies and all these things."],[947.57,"They're distractions. They're distractions."],[950.61,"Um, as we're told by the prophet, you know, what does the Lord require of you to do justly, to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God?"],[958.53,"And if you do that, you know, in your life, you're okay."],[962.45,"And that's what Jesus is telling his disciples here."],[965.33,"Don't worry about that stuff."],[967.19,"You don't need to worry about it."],[968.55,"Here's what you're called to do."],[970.31,"And you're gonna have plenty of work to do doing this."],[975.51,"And so focus."],[977.53,"Focus. And that's a good message for us because we have countless more distractions."],[980.33,"You know, the aforementioned Facebook and everything else"],[987.47,"If we want to get distracted, if we want to waste time, we have a thousand ways to do it."],[992.27,"You know, but there's work to be done that God has given us to do, and that needs to be our focus."],[1008.11,"And while they looked steadfastly toward heaven as he went up, behold, two men stood by them in white apparel."],[1014.03,"Who also said, Men of Galilee, why do you stand gazing up into heaven?"],[1018.03,"The same Jesus who was taken up from you into heaven will so come in like manner as you saw him go into heaven."],[1026.31,"So Jesus ascends into heaven, as we saw at the end of St."],[1031.35,"Luke's Gospel. And he disappears, disappears into a cloud until he disappears into a cloud."],[1039.11,"They can't see him anymore."],[1040.55,"And then two angels show up to sort of reinforce what Jesus just told them."],[1044.31,"Why are you standing here gawking?"],[1047.55,"Jesus is going to return."],[1049.81,"The same way you saw him depart."],[1051.81,"And implied, in the meantime, you have work to do."],[1057.09,"Yes, you have."],[1058.61,"He just told you what to do."],[1060.29,"Go do it."],[1061.17,"All right go Go do it."],[1067.25,"Then they returned to Jer Jerusalusemalem from the mount called Olivet, which is near, a Sabbath day's journey."],[1068.53,"Luke refers to a specific place"],[1073.45,"So notice again St."],[1076.17,"He gives you some details of geography."],[1078.78,"So this isn't just, you know, the wonderful story of when Jesus flew up into the sky."],[1083.6,"This is an actual event that he's placing in an actual place."],[1086.8,"You can follow his instructions."],[1090.72,"Go find it, go stand for where the where it was that Jesus ascended."],[1097.36,"And when they had had entered the city, they went up into the upper room where they were staying."],[1102.8,"Peter, James, John, and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James the son of Alpheus, and Simon the zealot, and Judas the son of James."],[1113.56,"So we've got the eleven disciples who are left now apostles."],[1117.88,"They go back to the room where they're staying."],[1120.6,"We're told this is the upper room, implying it's the same room where uh they had eaten the Last Supper."],[1129.02,"With Jesus. They're still staying, they're still staying in the same place."],[1133.98,"Um, they're all staying together, which is probably very economical."],[1140.62,"But it's not just these eleven."],[1142.46,"So we have the uh the eleven listed, but then also we're going to read these all continued with one accord in prayer and supplication, with the women and Mary, the mother of Jesus, and with his brothers."],[1155.58,"Okay. So it's it's not just the eleven, but the eleven and the women, meaning the merbearers."],[1163.79,"Mary, Martha, Joanna, the others, Salome, and Mary, the Theotokos, Christ's mother, and his brothers."],[1175.25,"Jesus' brothers. Notice that Jesus' brothers are there."],[1179.09,"The last time we saw Jesus' brothers in St."],[1181.01,"Luke's Gospel, they didn't believe him, and they were telling him to go home and knock it off and quit embarrassing the family."],[1188.37,"But now they're there."],[1189.97,"Now they believe."],[1190.85,"Why? Well, because Jesus has appeared to them since the resurrection."],[1196.61,"And uh while we we never have it narrated in the New Testament, St."],[1201.09,"Paul refers to it, the fact that Jesus appeared to James his brother"],[1208.25,"This would seem to be a result of that, since he's there and he now believes."],[1212.73,"But traditionally, when he appeared to him, he made him the first bishop of Jerusalem."],[1218.89,"He set him in charge of the church in Jerusalem."],[1222.65,"And we're going to see later in the book of Acts that St."],[1225.61,"James is very much in charge of the church in Jerusalem."],[1229.37,"So again, even though it's not narrated, we see him here believing now."],[1233.53,"We're going to see him in charge of the church in Jerusalem, and it's never going to tell us why him."],[1240.01,"And St. Paul is going to refer to the fact that Jesus appeared to him, but it's only from outside the biblical text that we have the tradition that that's because when Jesus appeared to him, he put him in that position."],[1255.65,"That is also going to, and we'll talk about this more later when St."],[1259.49,"James appears in that role, is going to cause certain problems for our Roman Catholic friends in terms of the role of Saint Peter, since he's not the one in charge."],[1270.93,"But we will get there."],[1276.61,"But so they're all gathered together."],[1278.45,"It's also important to note that the Theotokos is there."],[1282.77,"And then this is less our Roman Catholic friends and more of our Protestant friends, where they want to sort of write her off."],[1291.79,"That she sort of gives birth to Jesus and then becomes completely unimportant."],[1296.35,"And that is not the case."],[1298.53,"She's still here."],[1299.97,"And she's still a part of the community."],[1302.63,"She's right there with the eleven apostles."],[1304.31,"She's just as important."],[1305.6,"She's the only woman who's named, notice."],[1309.68,"Even Jesus' brothers, even St."],[1311.76,"James, who's about to become the leader of the is not mentioned by name here, but she is."],[1317.12,"So she's there."],[1318.4,"She's named, and the eleven disciples are named, the apostles are named."],[1322.56,"Meaning that to St."],[1323.76,"Luke, at least, she is just as significant as the eleven apostles."],[1328.88,"At least as significant as the eleven apostles."],[1331.84,"So that kind of mitigates against that, it is worth noticing here."],[1334.72,"In those days, Peter stood up in the midst of the disciples"],[1342.36,"Altogether, the number of names was about 120."],[1347.32,"Okay. So I don't know that I've talked about this here yet, but we see in St."],[1354.84,"Luke's Gospel and in the other, and in St."],[1357.8,"Matthew and St."],[1358.6,"Mark's Gospel, that Jesus sort of has these intersecting circles of followers."],[1365.72,"That there's the core group of the core group."],[1369.96,"Whenever we see Jesus go off by himself with just a couple of people, it's with St."],[1374.6,"Peter, St. James, and St."],[1376.2,"John. Those three sort of are the real tightener circle."],[1379.4,"the And then there's, of course, 12 disciples that those three are part of."],[1386.56,"And then we read about the 70 disciples, some of whom are going to be mentioned as apostles in the book of Acts."],[1395.84,"The 70 who Jesus sent out."],[1397.84,"And then there's this group of 120."],[1400.72,"And at this point, the whole church, the whole church of Christ is 120 people."],[1405.89,"All gathered together."],[1409.01,"And so these are the these are the remaining followers of Jesus."],[1417.65,"And so Peter stands up to address everybody."],[1423.41,"He says, Men and brethren, this scripture had to be fulfilled which the Holy Spirit spoke before by the mouth of David concerning Judas, who became a guide to those who arrested Jesus."],[1437.21,"For he was numbered with us and obtained a part in this ministry."],[1441.69,"Now he's going to continue to actually quote the passage, but just a couple things to notice here."],[1448.81,"Notice he says that the psalm he's about to quote was spoken by the Holy Spirit, by the mouth of David."],[1463.21,"So that shows us St."],[1464.97,"Peter's view of the scriptures."],[1469.13,"Or old books"],[1469.73,"So for him, the scriptures are not just a collection of ancient writings."],[1474.99,"This is the wisdom of our forefathers."],[1477.79,"The Psalms, oh, these are the hymns we like to sing in church."],[1481.87,"This is our hymnal."],[1483.71,"That's not it."],[1485.47,"For him, this is coming from coming from the Holy Spirit."],[1491.71,"This is spoken by the Holy Spirit."],[1493.31,"So these are these are the words of God."],[1496.11,"And this is what we reference, of course, in the Nicene Creed when we talk about the Holy Spirit who spake by the prophets."],[1501.81,"Who spoke through spoke through the prophets."],[1509.21,"And notice he's going to argue in the case of Judas."],[1514.27,"The case of Judas, the scripture had to be fulfilled."],[1517.71,"We talked about this with Judas a little bit in St."],[1521.15,"John's Gospel, but all of the gospel writers want to make it clear that Judas betraying Jesus was not because of some failure on Jesus' part."],[1533.31,"It wasn't that Jesus had wronged him in some way."],[1536.96,"Or that this had been a surprise to Jesus."],[1542.74,"That he had thought Judas was his good friend, and then Judas turned on him and he never saw it coming."],[1548.84,"Jesus knew about this."],[1550.12,"This was prophesied."],[1551.24,"This was something that had to happen."],[1554.14,"This betrayal was something that had to happen."],[1556.58,"It was the vehicle by which Christ was Christ laid down his life."],[1562.43,"So that he could he could rise again."],[1566.59,"And he mentions that Judas was numbered among them, numbered among the twelve, and obtained a portion of their ministry."],[1576.11,"Once again, Judas wasn't sort of a second class disciple."],[1579.63,"There were some meditations on this in Holy Week."],[1582.35,"You may have noticed."],[1585.19,"From Jesus' point of view, you know, what did I tell to the other disciples that I didn't tell to you?"],[1590.15,"What miracles did I give them to work that I didn't give to you?"],[1593.88,"And so Judas went and worked the same miracles as the other disciples."],[1598.2,"He went and baptized people with the other disciples."],[1600.92,"I've commented before, I always feel bad for those people who got baptized by Judas."],[1609.48,"But everything that the other disciples did, he did."],[1613.58,"From the point of view of Jesus, Jesus wronged him in no way."],[1618.72,"In no way."],[1622.24,"Now this man purchased a field with the wages of iniquity, and falling headlong, he burst open in the middle and all his entrails gushed out."],[1630.48,"So you can tell St."],[1631.92,"Peter doesn't have any lasting sympathy for Judas."],[1639.04,"Because we know Judas went and hung himself."],[1642.8,"But just that detail isn't enough for Saint Peter"],[1647.96,"He goes into a little more detail about what happened to the body."],[1654.52,"In some kind of some grisly detail."],[1659.08,"And it became known to all those dwelling in Jerusalem."],[1662.6,"So that field is called in their own language."],[1669.16,"That is the field of blood."],[1674.84,"The field of blood."],[1676.06,"And we already read that story about the purchase of that property, the Potter's Field."],[1683.26,"For it is written in the book of Psalms: let his dwelling place be desolate, and let no one live in it, and let another take his office."],[1687.5,"Let another take his office"],[1694.74,"Interestingly, in the in the Greek, it literally says, Let no one let another one take his episcopacy."],[1702.98,"It uses the word episcopos, which we translate as bishop."],[1710.34,"And you can go back and read uh the psalm that that's quoted from, uh, which is Psalm uh 69."],[1720.34,"Um the first part of Psalm 69, second part of Psalm 109, both of those discuss uh betrayal by a close friend."],[1729.35,"And so, as we mentioned before, when when the New Testament authors quote a line from a verse of scripture, they're not just sort of like, oh, look, I found something."],[1738.43,"I could pull out of context and come into use."],[1741.55,"They're referring to the whole the whole psalm, the whole context."],[1747.71,"Remember where it said that?"],[1748.99,"Okay, go back and read that."],[1750.59,"And you'll see that this picture of Judas's betrayal was laid out far in advance."],[1757.17,"Far in advance."],[1758.53,"And so this wasn't a surprise."],[1760.21,"This wasn't a failure of Jesus."],[1761.81,"This was something that happened exactly in accordance with what had been prophesied through David."],[1770.37,"And so now he's saying Judas has sort of received the recompense. for what he did"],[1778.73,"And part of that, because the toothpieces he quotes come after the betrayal in those Psalms."],[1784.59,"It's the consequence."],[1786.51,"And it actually goes into even more detail than that."],[1788.67,"The let his dwelling place be desolate, let no one live in it."],[1791.39,"Talks about all his children being barren, so his family line ends with him."],[1797.07,"I mean, it goes into some detail about the curse that would come upon him."],[1804.75,"But so uh St."],[1806.19,"Peter is saying, you know, that first part was fulfilled, he betrayed Jesus."],[1810.48,"And now he's dead."],[1812.48,"Now the rest of this is, you know, that someone else needs to take his position, his office, his role among the twelve apostles."],[1829.0,"Therefore, of these men who have accompanied us all the time that the Lord Jesus went in and out among us, beginning from the baptism of John to that day when he was taken up from us, one of these must become a witness with us of his resurrection."],[1844.2,"Notice again what the role of the apostles is, according to Saint Peter."],[1851.82,"Must become, not must become a leader."],[1854.99,"Not must become an authority, not must become a member of our council."],[1859.44,"But must become a witness with us of his resurrection."],[1862.96,"That's what he sent them out to do"],[1863.96,"Because Rebe, Jesus said, You will be my witnesses."],[1868.82,"He said, You've been with me this whole time, you've seen everything I've done, you've heard everything I taught, you saw me die, you saw me alive, and resurrected."],[1879.95,"You're to go out and bear witness to this and proclaim this."],[1882.69,"And so Saint Peter says, We need a twelfth person to do that."],[1887.81,"And so because that's the job, it has to be someone who's been with us this whole time, who can bear witness to all of these things."],[1899.53,"And they proposed to Joseph called Barsabbas, who was surnamed Justice, and Matthias."],[1908.01,"And they prayed and said, You, O Lord, who know the hearts of all, show which of these two you have chosen to take part in this ministry, an apostleship from which Judas by transgression fell, that he might go to his own place."],[1924.33,"More literally in Greek, it says that he may go where he belongs."],[1928.38,"So Judas is the one person who in scripture we're told went to hell. but Judas uh here, St"],[1939.86,"Peter said, went to hell, which is the place he belongs."],[1943.5,"But notice again the ministry and apostleship, which Judas had."],[1950.54,"Judas was a witness to all of those things."],[1951.1,"was. He there"],[1953.86,"He saw Jesus, he heard everything Jesus taught."],[1957.03,"But he transgressed, he sinned."],[1958.95,"Because of his own sin, he fell from that."],[1961.19,"He lost that."],[1963.43,"So now we need someone to replace him."],[1967.03,"And they cast their lots, and the lot fell on Matthias, and he was numbered with the eleven apostles."],[1974.87,"What's a lot?"],[1976.63,"Okay. Throwing dice."],[1981.27,"It's based upon in the Old Testament."],[1984.99,"In the in the Torah, in the Pentateuch, uh, there were these two stones called the Urim and the Thummim."],[1992.23,"And they were kept in pockets of the ephod of the breast piece of the high high priest."],[1998.11,"And we're not sure exactly what was done with them."],[2001.15,"Something was done with these two stones."],[2004.35,"They were thrown or rolled or dropped or and in some way, based on the way they landed or the way they sat, that would decide cases."],[2017.23,"And so essentially what it says in the Torah, in the Pentateuch, is if you have a decision to make and you're seeking sort of God's will, and it's not clear."],[2029.33,"Most things are pretty clear."],[2031.57,"You know, you read the law."],[2032.85,"God didn't want them doing like divination and horoscopes and right that kind of thing to try and solve these things."],[2039.81,"So he said, look, if if honestly you can't tell."],[2043.54,"If you've got an honest, you can't tell, then you have the high priest use the urum and the thumbum, and that will that that will give you your answer and do it that way."],[2059.22,"And so this practice of casting lots, and again, we don't know exactly how it worked again, if it was dice or chips, or exactly how exactly what they did, but it was some kind of chance thing like that."],[2074.26,"Like the way we would flip a coin today."],[2076.42,"It was some kind of chance thing like that, which they believed would then tell them"],[2084.02,"Now, one of the interesting things about this event."],[2087.98,"Saint Matthias is considered a saint."],[2090.22,"He's even called an apostle by the church."],[2094.06,"But all the members of the 70 are referred to as apostles by the church."],[2099.9,"Which he must have been also."],[2104.06,"But you may notice when you see depictions of the 12 apostles in the church, like on our iconostasis."],[2111.26,"Alright, we have the 12 apostles in the second row."],[2114.38,"Or when you see the icon of Pentecost with the 12 apostles."],[2119.02,"Saint Matthias isn't there"],[2124.98,"Have you noticed who the 12th person is?"],[2127.42,"No who? St."],[2129.06,"Saint Paul. Paul"],[2129.5,"Paul. Saint Even in the icon of Pentecost when Saint Paul was not there."],[2140.26,"Because Saint Paul was not a follower of Christ at the time that the Pentecost happened."],[2147.52,"The Holy Spirit came."],[2149.44,"And so. Part of what Saint Luke is doing here in the Acts of the Apostles."],[2159.49,"And I think he's paralleling this with something I'll talk about in a second from the Old Testament."],[2166.13,"But is, you know, it doesn't say, no one told Saint Peter to do this."],[2173.25,"Peter was filled with the Holy Spirit and stood up and right"],[2173.9,"Doesn't say St."],[2178.3,"Jesus didn't tell them to do that."],[2179.82,"Oh, by the way, select someone."],[2183.42,"I was thinking about, I was going to ask that question."],[2185.66,"Why would Saint Peter be the one that took the state?"],[2188.12,"No one, no one told him to do that."],[2190.92,"No one told the apostles to do that."],[2192.68,"Jesus told them to just wait for the Holy Spirit."],[2196.2,"And so I believe, without saying anything negative about St."],[2200.6,"Matthias, who is a saint and is an apostle."],[2204.61,"In the way that all the 70 are apostles."],[2206.69,"So I don't want it to sound like that."],[2209.41,"It seems clear that what St."],[2210.77,"Luke is doing here is saying that they sort of went ahead and did this, but God already had someone in mind, to be the 12th."],[2222.39,"And it wasn't somebody who the other other 11 ever would have picked."],[2228.92,"But he's the one who Christ picked and appeared to and made an apostle."],[2236.28,"And made an apostle."],[2245.0,"In her tradition, by depicting St."],[2248.52,"Paul as the 12th."],[2251.96,"In the 12 Apostles, the icon of the Twelve Aostples, the Twelve Apostles of the Achotostas, even the icon of Pentecost."],[2260.68,"Paul who Christ selected to be"],[2261.04,"That it's St."],[2261.76,"Paul who's the 12th, because it's St."],[2267.44,"Selected to be the 12th."],[2269.12,"So Saint Peter doesn't get to ordain whoever he wants."],[2274.64,"Contra. Contra our uh Roman Catholic friends."],[2288.48,"Well, is that really out of character for Saint Peter?"],[2291.2,"As we've seen him in the Gospels."],[2295.66,"Jumping out of the boat?"],[2296.78,"Yeah. And then looking around and getting scared and sinking."],[2300.04,"Or, you know, when Jesus says, You're all gonna abandon me, and he says, I'll die before I abandon you, you know."],[2305.72,"Saint Peter, yeah"],[2307.36,"And, you know, that's pretty consistent with his character."],[2313.12,"So uh and and I think Saint Luke is is subtly drawing a comparison to another episode in the Old Testament that involves someone else named Saul, namely Saul and David."],[2331.12,"The end of Deuteronomy, when God uh talks about them having a king."],[2336.85,"The end of Deuteronomy, God gives a lot of very negative predictions about what's going to happen to Israel."],[2341.81,"He predicts they're gonna end up going into exile, for example."],[2345.09,"He tells them, When you have transgressed my law and you've done all this evil, I'm going to send you into exile."],[2350.21,"He knows they're going to have a king"],[2350.81,"He also says, when you have a king, even though in Samuel he's going to say, you really don't want a king, you really don't want a king."],[2358.09,"And in Deuteronomy, he says, When you have a king, wait for the king who I will choose."],[2366.57,"But what do we see in the book of 1 Samuel?"],[2368.65,"Well, they decide, we want a king like the other nations have kings."],[2373.07,"They all have kings."],[2374.83,"We want a king like the other nations."],[2377.79,"And God says, No, you don't."],[2380.75,"Because he's going to tax you."],[2382.35,"He's going to draft your sons in the military and send them off to die."],[2386.19,"He's going to, you know, take your daughters for his wives and have all this hero."],[2390.43,"You know, he's going to do all these things."],[2391.79,"You really don't want to, you want me to be your king."],[2394.11,"You don't want a king like the nations have."],[2394.43,"want They say, no, we a king."],[2394.67,"They choose Saul"],[2398.45,"And so who do they choose?"],[2400.29,"Why? Well, because he's a head taller than everybody else."],[2403.81,"He's this big strapping guy."],[2406.29,"Saul of the Old Testament."],[2407.43,"He's this big strapping guy."],[2410.04,"Big tough guy."],[2411.16,"Oh, yeah, this guy."],[2412.6,"He'll intimidate, you know."],[2414.65,"They choose him, and it's a disaster."],[2417.23,"And who does God choose?"],[2419.93,"The least likely person."],[2421.05,"Remember, he sends Samuel to anoint the king."],[2423.21,"Jesse brings all his sons out."],[2426.11,"He walks up to the oldest son, you know, big big guy."],[2429.95,"God says, Nope, not him."],[2431.65,"Sort of works his way down."],[2433.41,"Nope, nope, nope, nope, nope."],[2435.01,"He says, You got any other sons?"],[2435.57,"got He says, Yeah, well, I this little run."],[2438.81,"He's off taking care of the sheep."],[2443.29,"God says, That's the one."],[2445.38,"That's the one who I picked."],[2447.16,"The last one you'd expect."],[2448.68,"We see the same thing happening here."],[2453.54,"The one who he picks, Saul, who becomes St."],[2456.58,"Paul, is the last person they ever would have picked."],[2460.43,"Persecuting the church."],[2462.67,"We know he's uh we know he's not good looking."],[2466.99,"We have a physical description of him."],[2469.07,"And he went into the from around the time he l he was very short, he was bald, he had a severe eye condition where pus ran into his eyes all the time that's where he could barely see he was almost blind uh he's described as being bow legged on a money so he he was not he was not again the good looking you know this is this is the charismatic guy who I want to put out there as our uh our preacher to go out to all the Gentiles and you know win people over to Christianity right not to mention the fact that he you know hated the church and was persecuting it was was going out and having Christians killed, getting mobs to stone Christians like St."],[2514.63,"Stephen to death."],[2516.03,"But but there was nothing physically about him."],[2519.07,"He was he was a little rabbi."],[2521.81,"Jewish scholar. Who had studied all these things."],[2525.58,"And you know, but that's who God chose to be Saint Paul, you know, who is going to become the main character of this book by the time we're done."],[2538.28,"And, you know, Saint Paul is going to reference this a lot of times."],[2542.76,"In fact, at one point he references his nickname."],[2545.72,"His opponents referred to him as the abortion."],[2550.6,"Because that's how unattractive he looked."],[2555.32,"They said he was that he he must have they must have tried to kill him in the womb, because that's how he came out that way."],[2576.88,"But he's gonna refer to you know uh the the himself and the other apostles as sort of the off-scourings of the universe."],[2585.44,"He's gonna, you know, and talks about God placing his treasures and earthen vessels, you know, not in sort of your big gold."],[2592.24,"You know. Um he's talking about himself."],[2596.56,"He's talking about himself."],[2598.8,"Um but so that gives all of us hope."],[2603.2,"God can do great things through us, too."],[2605.84,"Um but uh, but yeah, so so that is that is going on in the background here."],[2611.28,"here. We're gonna see, you know, we see St"],[2614.76,"Peter sort of jump ahead and choose someone, but we're gonna see as the book goes on who it is who God chooses."],[2625.64,"So we're at the end of chapter one, so this is probably a good place to stop for this evening."],[2631.32,"So thank you, everybody."],[2633.64,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2640.92,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2646.28,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.64,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:1-2 - Dedication to Theophilus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"The former account\"</b> = Gospel of Luke, volume one</li><li class=\"d0\">Summarized as \"all that Jesus <b>began</b> both to <b>do and teach</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus has ascended - Acts not more of Jesus doing and teaching directly</li><li class=\"d0\">Setup: what the apostles now do and teach = the <b>Acts and deeds</b> of Christ's teaching</li><li class=\"d1\">they are his <b>representatives</b></li><li class=\"d1\">work of <b>salvation continues</b> through the apostles</li><li class=\"d0\">Church life = <b>continuation</b> of Christ's mission, not a separate thing</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"Israel, then Jesus, then church\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Against <b>red-letter</b> idea: what <b>Paul, Peter, James</b> teach are the teachings of Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not something new or added to or different\"</li></ul>"},{"t":159.29,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:3 - Infallible proofs over 40 days","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jesus presented himself alive <b>after his suffering</b> by <b>many infallible proofs</b>, <b>40 days</b>, speaking of the <b>kingdom of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Luke's <b>appeal to evidence</b> for the resurrection</li><li class=\"d1\">not just visions - common in the ancient world and today (\"I swear I saw him in my bedroom\")</li><li class=\"d1\">Luke: \"that's not what I'm talking about\"</li><li class=\"d0\">End of Luke: <b>\"see my hands and my feet\"</b>, \"handle me and see\"</li><li class=\"d1\">spirit has no <b>flesh and blood</b>; not a ghost, not a hallucination</li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus <b>eats food</b> in front of them</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul will add a list of witnesses: <b>500 at once</b>, \"many still alive, go ask them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"History, reality, not visions\": dead, buried, then alive - <b>eating, talking, walking</b></li></ul>"},{"t":330.33,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:4-5 - Wait for the promise","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Commanded <b>not to depart Jerusalem</b>, wait for <b>the promise of the Father</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"John baptized with water, you shall be baptized with the <b>Holy Spirit</b> not many days from now\"</li><li class=\"d0\">During the 40 days he taught them about the kingdom</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Emmaus road</b>: explained all the law and prophets concerning himself</li><li class=\"d1\">parables in his life; even in <b>John</b> (plain speech) disciples \"clueless\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>understood only after the resurrection</b> - he finishes the teaching</li><li class=\"d0\">Last directive: \"sending you out, but <b>don't go yet</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">refers back to <b>John the Baptist</b>: baptize with the Spirit and fire</li></ul>"},{"t":445.76,"lv":3,"h":"The prophetic background of the Spirit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Promised in the prophets</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Joel 2</b> - Peter's Pentecost sermon: \"last days I'll pour out my Spirit on <b>all flesh</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Ezekiel</b> - new covenant: \"I'm going to place my Spirit in you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Promise for the <b>last days</b>, new covenant, after Messiah comes</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus explained these OT scriptures to them</li><li class=\"d1\">promise \"from centuries past\" now coming to fruition</li></ul>"},{"t":512.14,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:6-8 - Restore the kingdom to Israel?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: \"Lord, will you at this time <b>restore the kingdom to Israel</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">looks like they don't get it - but the question <b>makes sense</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jeremiah, Ezekiel, Joel</b> tie new covenant Spirit to the <b>kingdom of God</b> established</li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit promise coming true → \"is the other part?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus' answer: \"not for you to know <b>times or seasons</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't say \"you still don't get it\" or \"my kingdom is not of this world, there is no kingdom\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"You shall receive <b>power</b> when the Holy Spirit has come... <b>witnesses</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jerusalem</b>, all <b>Judea</b>, <b>Samaria</b>, <b>ends of the earth</b></li></ul>"},{"t":600.75,"lv":3,"h":"What the kingdom question meant","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not \"now overthrow the Romans\"</li><li class=\"d0\">The kingdom of God <b>already exists</b> - Christ rules, <b>enthroned after the ascension</b></li><li class=\"d1\">manifest in the <b>church</b>, wherever Christ is</li><li class=\"d1\">kingdoms of this world (<b>Rome</b>) still exist, mostly <b>opposed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Restore the kingdom\" = the <b>end</b>: kingdom of God becomes the whole world</li><li class=\"d1\">heaven and earth become one at Christ's return</li><li class=\"d0\">Their misunderstanding: <b>time gap</b> between resurrection and the end</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Last days\": Paul and others call the present time the last days</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Are we in the end times?\" - yes, for <b>1980 years</b></li><li class=\"d1\">last age before the <b>age to come</b></li></ul>"},{"t":736.14,"lv":2,"h":"The mission plan: be witnesses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"You don't get to know how long\" - what you need: receive power, <b>be my witnesses</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Plan for the rest of Acts: <b>Jerusalem</b> → <b>Judea</b> (Roman province) → <b>Samaria</b> (neighboring) → <b>ends of the earth</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"This is your mission, what's set before you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Message for us: not just <b>end-time date-setting</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>2012 Mayan calendar</b>, year <b>2000</b> - \"I've lived through 10 or 12 ends of the world\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Cerebral Westerners with <b>free time</b> to speculate</li></ul>"},{"t":850.06,"lv":3,"h":"Distractions vs what God requires","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ancient farmer: sunup to sundown, five or six kids, <b>no time to speculate</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now: argue on <b>Facebook</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Temptation to <b>pry and theorize</b> - churches divide over <b>six literal days</b> or periods in Genesis</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they're a distraction\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"What does the Lord really require?\" - pretty straightforward</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: <b>genealogies, myths, philosophies</b> = distractions</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Micah</b>: do justly, love mercy, walk humbly with your God</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus: \"don't worry about that stuff\" - plenty of work to do</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Focus</b> - countless more distractions today; work God has given us</li></ul>"},{"t":1008.11,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:9-12 - The Ascension","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two men in white: \"<b>Men of Galilee</b>, why do you stand gazing up?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus disappears into a <b>cloud</b>; angels reinforce</li><li class=\"d1\">\"why are you standing here gawking?\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>same Jesus</b> will return <b>the same way</b></li><li class=\"d1\">implied: in the meantime <b>you have work to do</b> - \"Go do it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Return from <b>Mount Olivet</b>, a <b>Sabbath day's journey</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Luke gives <b>geography</b> - actual event in an actual place</li><li class=\"d1\">\"go stand where Jesus ascended\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1097.36,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:13-14 - The upper room","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Entered the city, <b>upper room</b> where staying</li><li class=\"d1\">likely same as the <b>Last Supper</b> room</li><li class=\"d0\">Eleven named: <b>Peter, James, John, Andrew, Philip, Thomas, Bartholomew, Matthew, James son of Alpheus, Simon the Zealot, Judas son of James</b></li><li class=\"d1\">staying together - \"probably very economical\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just the eleven: \"one accord in prayer\" with the <b>women</b> (myrrh-bearers)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Mary, Martha, Joanna, Salome</b>, and <b>Mary the Theotokos</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1175.25,"lv":3,"h":"Jesus' brothers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Last seen in <b>Luke</b>: didn't believe, \"go home, quit embarrassing the family\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now they <b>believe</b> - because Jesus <b>appeared to them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">never narrated; <b>Paul</b> refers to Jesus appearing to <b>James his brother</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tradition: made him <b>first bishop of Jerusalem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">later in Acts <b>James is in charge</b> of the church there - never says why</li><li class=\"d1\">only <b>outside the text</b> the tradition</li><li class=\"d0\">Causes problems for <b>Roman Catholic</b> friends re: <b>Peter</b> - not the one in charge</li><li class=\"d1\">\"we will get there\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1276.61,"lv":3,"h":"The Theotokos present","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Against <b>Protestants</b> who write her off - gives birth, then unimportant</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not the case\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Still part of the community, with the eleven</li><li class=\"d0\">The <b>only woman named</b></li><li class=\"d1\">even <b>James</b> not named, but she is</li><li class=\"d0\">To Luke at least as significant as the <b>eleven apostles</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1334.72,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:15 - The 120 and circles of followers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"In those days Peter stood up\" - about <b>120</b> names</li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus' <b>intersecting circles</b> of followers</li><li class=\"d1\">innermost: <b>Peter, James, John</b> - when he goes off with a few</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>12</b> they belong to</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>70</b> sent out - some called apostles in Acts</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>120</b> - \"the whole church of Christ is 120 people\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1417.65,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:16-17 - Peter on Scripture and Judas","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Peter: scripture \"had to be fulfilled\" which the <b>Holy Spirit spoke by the mouth of David</b> concerning Judas</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter's view of Scripture: not \"wisdom of our forefathers\" or \"our hymnal\"</li><li class=\"d1\">spoken by the <b>Holy Spirit</b> = <b>words of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Nicene Creed</b>: \"who spoke by the prophets\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Gospel writers: Judas' betrayal not Jesus' <b>failure</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a wrong done to Judas; no surprise; prophesied</li><li class=\"d1\">vehicle by which Christ <b>laid down his life</b> to rise again</li><li class=\"d0\">Judas <b>numbered among the twelve</b>, obtained a share</li><li class=\"d1\">worked the same <b>miracles</b>, baptized - \"I feel bad for those baptized by Judas\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus wronged him \"in no way\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1622.24,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:18-20 - Judas' end and the Psalms","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Bought a field with the <b>wages of iniquity</b>, burst open, entrails gushed out</li><li class=\"d1\">Peter has <b>no lasting sympathy</b>; adds grisly detail to the hanging</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Akeldama</b> = <b>field of blood</b>; the Potter's Field</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Let another take his office\" - Greek <i>episkopen</i> = <b>episcopacy</b>, bishop</li><li class=\"d0\">From <b>Psalm 69</b> (first part) and <b>Psalm 109</b> (second part): betrayal by a close friend</li><li class=\"d1\">NT quotes the <b>whole psalm</b>, whole context - \"go back and read\"</li><li class=\"d1\">betrayal laid out far in advance</li><li class=\"d0\">Quotes from after the betrayal = <b>consequence</b>: desolate dwelling, <b>children barren</b>, family line ends</li><li class=\"d0\">First part fulfilled; now <b>someone else takes his office</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1829.0,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 1:21-26 - Choosing Matthias","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Must have accompanied them from the <b>baptism of John</b> to the ascension</li><li class=\"d0\">Role of an apostle: \"become a <b>witness with us of his resurrection</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not leader, authority, council member</li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus: \"you will be my witnesses\"; must have been there the whole time</li><li class=\"d0\">Proposed: <b>Joseph called Barsabbas</b> (surnamed <b>Justice</b>) and <b>Matthias</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Prayer: \"Lord who know the hearts of all\"; Judas fell \"by transgression\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Greek: \"go where he <b>belongs</b>\" - the one person Scripture says went to <b>hell</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Judas was witness too - lost it by <b>his own sin</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Lot fell on Matthias, numbered with the eleven</li></ul>"},{"t":1974.87,"lv":3,"h":"Casting lots","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Throwing dice - basis in the <b>Torah</b>: <b>Urim and Thummim</b></li><li class=\"d1\">two stones in the high priest's <b>ephod / breast piece</b></li><li class=\"d1\">thrown or rolled - \"we're not sure exactly\"</li><li class=\"d0\">For decisions when God's will isn't clear</li><li class=\"d1\">most things clear in the law - <b>no divination, horoscopes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if you honestly can't tell, high priest uses them</li><li class=\"d0\">Some chance thing \"like flipping a coin\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2084.02,"lv":2,"h":"Matthias and the real twelfth apostle","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Matthias</b> is a saint, called an apostle - as all the <b>70</b> are</li><li class=\"d0\">Icons of the 12 (iconostasis, <b>Pentecost</b>) don't show Matthias - the 12th is <b>St. Paul</b></li><li class=\"d1\">even in Pentecost, when Paul wasn't yet a follower</li><li class=\"d0\">No one told Peter to do this; Jesus said <b>just wait</b> for the Spirit</li><li class=\"d1\">without disrespect to Matthias - Luke: they <b>went ahead</b>, but God had someone in mind</li><li class=\"d1\">not whom the eleven would pick - <b>Christ picked and appeared to him</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Peter doesn't get to ordain whoever he wants\" - <b>contra Roman Catholic</b> friends</li><li class=\"d0\">In character for Peter: <b>jumping out of the boat</b>, sinking; \"I'll die before I abandon you\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2313.12,"lv":3,"h":"Saul and David parallel","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Luke subtly compares another <b>Saul</b> - <b>Saul and David</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>End of Deuteronomy</b>: predicts exile; \"when you have a king, wait for the king <b>I will choose</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Samuel</b>: \"we want a king like the other nations\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God: he'll <b>tax</b> you, <b>draft your sons</b>, take daughters</li><li class=\"d1\">they choose <b>Saul</b> - a head taller, \"big strapping guy\" → disaster</li><li class=\"d0\">God chooses the <b>least likely</b>: Samuel, <b>Jesse's sons</b>, \"nope, nope\"</li><li class=\"d1\">youngest, off with the <b>sheep</b> - \"that's the one\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same here: <b>Saul/Paul</b> last person they'd pick - persecuting the church</li></ul>"},{"t":2462.67,"lv":2,"h":"Paul: the least likely twelfth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Physical description: <b>short, bald</b>, eye condition (pus), nearly blind, <b>bow-legged</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not the charismatic preacher to win the Gentiles</li><li class=\"d0\">Hated the church, <b>mobs stoned Stephen</b>; \"a little rabbi\", Jewish scholar</li><li class=\"d0\">Becomes <b>main character</b> of the book</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul references it: opponents' nickname <b>\"the abortion\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so unattractive - \"tried to kill him in the womb\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Calls apostles <b>off-scourings of the universe</b>; <b>treasure in earthen vessels</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"God can do great things through us, too\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter jumps ahead; we'll see <b>who God chooses</b></li><li class=\"d0\">End of chapter 1</li></ul>"}]});
